\ Standalone AOT lint driver: the same bootstrap the `1z lint` subcommand
\ runs through the interpreter, against a fixed fixture, so the compiled
\ tokenize / lint path can be built ahead-of-time. The harness passes no argv
\ to AOT binaries, so the target path is embedded rather than read from
\ `command-line-args`.
\
\ This is a build-only test: the runtime-image driver compiles, but running it
\ hits a separate, pre-existing AOT runtime-image execution bug in the full
\ run-lint path (a scanner reaches `>` where a number is expected), tracked in
\ spec/bugs/. Once that is fixed this becomes a run-and-match test against
\ interpreted `1z lint`.
use "lint" ;
use "lint-rules" ;
{ "tests/fixtures/lint/unused-import.1z" } run-lint [ 0 ] [ 1 ] if sys-exit
